WEBVTT

1
01:00:05.005 --> 01:00:07.842
All these gifts
you have given me.

2
01:00:08.309 --> 01:00:09.643
New clothes.

3
01:00:09.710 --> 01:00:11.679
A new home.

4
01:00:11.745 --> 01:00:14.248
With these. I can land
on my feet again.

5
01:00:14.315 --> 01:00:17.251
So. for my last wish.

6
01:00:17.318 --> 01:00:18.986
All Powerful Genie.

7
01:00:19.053 --> 01:00:22.256
I'll wish for your freedom.

8
01:00:25.594 --> 01:00:26.894
You mean it?

9
01:00:26.961 --> 01:00:28.095
It's the least I could do

10
01:00:28.162 --> 01:00:30.631
for all you've done
for me.

11
01:00:30.698 --> 01:00:32.299
I'll wish you free.

12
01:00:32.366 --> 01:00:34.668
[magical whirring]

13
01:00:43.377 --> 01:00:45.880
Ah! Thank you!

14
01:00:47.748 --> 01:00:50.619
Thank you. Gary.
Thank you so much.

15
01:00:50.684 --> 01:00:53.954
[chuckling]

16
01:00:54.021 --> 01:00:56.223
I hope you like it
in here.

17
01:00:56.290 --> 01:00:58.292
[magical whirring]

18
01:00:59.827 --> 01:01:02.531
What's this?

19
01:01:02.597 --> 01:01:05.099
What's happening to me?

20
01:01:05.166 --> 01:01:07.536
[sputtering]

21
01:01:07.602 --> 01:01:09.270
[screams]

22
01:01:10.771 --> 01:01:13.207
I tried to make it
very comfy in there.

23
01:01:13.274 --> 01:01:15.242
Enjoy.

24
01:01:18.712 --> 01:01:20.549
For me?

25
01:01:20.615 --> 01:01:22.149
[happily humming]

26
01:01:22.216 --> 01:01:24.018
Good morning.

27
01:01:25.419 --> 01:01:27.321
[photo snaps]

28
01:01:29.524 --> 01:01:31.325
[deep breath. sings]

29
01:01:31.392 --> 01:01:35.062
<i>[theme music]</i>

30
01:01:41.570 --> 01:01:44.071
Okay. now that we're
all appropriately caffeinated.

31
01:01:44.138 --> 01:01:46.073
we have things to discuss.

32
01:01:47.208 --> 01:01:49.076
- Yes. we do.
- Mm-hmm.

33
01:01:49.143 --> 01:01:51.745
- Which is?
- Well. Charlie and I think

34
01:01:51.812 --> 01:01:53.113
it'd be a good idea to go over

35
01:01:53.180 --> 01:01:54.982
some of our recent adventures
and take stock.

36
01:01:55.049 --> 01:01:57.818
I thought we'd been
performing admirably together.

37
01:01:57.885 --> 01:01:59.153
Oh. we have.

38
01:01:59.220 --> 01:02:01.255
But Charlie and Liza
are right.

39
01:02:01.322 --> 01:02:03.625
Sometimes it's worthwhile
just to check in

40
01:02:03.692 --> 01:02:05.893
before tensions get built up.

41
01:02:05.960 --> 01:02:08.095
And spill out in
opportune times.

42
01:02:08.162 --> 01:02:11.700
Ah. like our little angry.
demonic friend at the school.

43
01:02:11.765 --> 01:02:13.901
Well. yes. I can see
the advantages

44
01:02:13.968 --> 01:02:15.169
of such an endeavor.

45
01:02:15.236 --> 01:02:16.470
And very intelligent to hold

46
01:02:16.538 --> 01:02:18.607
this meeting in
a neutral space. Charlie.

47
01:02:18.673 --> 01:02:21.475
It may help
to keep more...

48
01:02:21.543 --> 01:02:23.043
extreme reactions in check.

49
01:02:23.110 --> 01:02:24.144
I am sitting right here.

50
01:02:24.211 --> 01:02:25.746
Sound managerial strategy.

51
01:02:25.813 --> 01:02:27.414
one I have observed
many times.

52
01:02:27.481 --> 01:02:29.783
But you've never worked
with a group before.

53
01:02:29.850 --> 01:02:31.752
No. but now that
you are on my team.

54
01:02:31.819 --> 01:02:33.420
I have taken to watching
I management videos

55
01:02:33.487 --> 01:02:35.256
on the YouTube.

56
01:02:35.322 --> 01:02:37.659
On your team?

57
01:02:37.726 --> 01:02:38.993
I am the Senior Librarian.

58
01:02:39.059 --> 01:02:40.327
therefore the head
of this team.

59
01:02:40.394 --> 01:02:42.329
- Okay. Mr. Senior.
- You are not in charge.

60
01:02:42.396 --> 01:02:43.931
You wouldn't have survived
the first week

61
01:02:43.998 --> 01:02:45.232
if it weren't for me.

62
01:02:47.434 --> 01:02:49.136
Back for more?
Already?

63
01:02:49.203 --> 01:02:52.106
Of course.
Hot chocolate is the best.

64
01:02:52.172 --> 01:02:54.542
and yours is the best
in the city.

65
01:02:54.609 --> 01:02:55.809
Oh. thank you.

66
01:02:55.876 --> 01:02:56.910
I will send it to you.

67
01:02:56.977 --> 01:02:57.978
Thank you.

68
01:02:58.045 --> 01:03:00.080
No. I'll be there.

69
01:03:00.147 --> 01:03:01.683
I just wish I could
find my keys.

70
01:03:01.750 --> 01:03:04.351
[shimmer]

71
01:03:04.418 --> 01:03:06.554
Um. miss?

72
01:03:06.621 --> 01:03:07.788
Are these your keys?

73
01:03:07.855 --> 01:03:09.456
Yeah.

74
01:03:10.791 --> 01:03:13.460
I have held the role
longest as anyone here.

75
01:03:13.528 --> 01:03:14.795
Okay. Vic. we love you.

76
01:03:14.862 --> 01:03:16.230
but you were in a time bubble

77
01:03:16.297 --> 01:03:18.667
for 175 of those years.
I don't think they count.

78
01:03:18.733 --> 01:03:20.100
Even discounting those years.

79
01:03:20.167 --> 01:03:21.902
I had a decade
to learn the ropes.

80
01:03:21.969 --> 01:03:23.971
And yes. there are ropes
to learn.

81
01:03:24.038 --> 01:03:25.372
And you think
you don't have ropes?

82
01:03:25.439 --> 01:03:27.041
You still barely know how
to use your phone.

83
01:03:27.107 --> 01:03:29.076
Yeah. and I keep trying
to teach you email. but...

84
01:03:29.143 --> 01:03:30.377
That is irrelevant.
I have grasped

85
01:03:30.444 --> 01:03:31.845
the responsibility
of our station--

86
01:03:31.912 --> 01:03:36.283
Hold on. everyone.
"Responsibility?"

87
01:03:36.350 --> 01:03:38.385
Ooh. delicious.

88
01:03:38.452 --> 01:03:40.020
Thank you.

89
01:03:41.155 --> 01:03:43.123
MAN: Look. I'm sorry.

90
01:03:43.190 --> 01:03:44.892
I wish you say that
to my mother.

91
01:03:44.958 --> 01:03:46.827
[shimmer]

92
01:03:46.894 --> 01:03:49.029
[cell phone ringing]

93
01:03:50.497 --> 01:03:52.667
Uh. i-- it's your mother.

94
01:03:52.734 --> 01:03:54.569
[ringing continues]

95
01:03:56.470 --> 01:03:58.005
Um. hello?

96
01:03:59.541 --> 01:04:01.543
Vikram. I'm sorry.
but responsibility

97
01:04:01.609 --> 01:04:03.844
isn't often something we
associate with you.

98
01:04:03.911 --> 01:04:05.112
Yeah. no.

99
01:04:05.179 --> 01:04:06.581
It's more agent of chaos.

100
01:04:06.648 --> 01:04:08.583
Remember when you got us
stuck in medieval times?

101
01:04:08.650 --> 01:04:10.017
You got shot by Cupid's arrow?

102
01:04:10.084 --> 01:04:12.152
You trusted Merlin.
and now. Mrs. A

103
01:04:12.219 --> 01:04:13.887
is off somewhere trying
to hunt him down.

104
01:04:13.954 --> 01:04:15.889
We all trusted him.
and chaos is something

105
01:04:15.956 --> 01:04:17.358
that happens in this job.

106
01:04:17.424 --> 01:04:19.293
You are all wonderful.
lovely people.

107
01:04:19.360 --> 01:04:21.862
but you are not yet
fully aware of the myriad

108
01:04:21.929 --> 01:04:23.097
a Librarian must face.

109
01:04:23.163 --> 01:04:24.766
If I am to be bound to anyone.

110
01:04:24.833 --> 01:04:26.735
I sometimes wish it was to

111
01:04:26.801 --> 01:04:28.670
a Librarian
of more experience.

112
01:04:28.737 --> 01:04:30.204
[shimmer]

113
01:04:30.270 --> 01:04:32.406
Throw me the idol!
Throw...

114
01:04:36.377 --> 01:04:37.645
Charlie?

115
01:04:39.781 --> 01:04:41.315
Vikram?

116
01:04:44.084 --> 01:04:46.821
What the hell am I
doing in Belgrade?

117
01:04:46.887 --> 01:04:48.857
♪♪♪

118
01:04:48.922 --> 01:04:50.592
It could be
a matter transference.

119
01:04:50.658 --> 01:04:52.059
More likely an effect
to the object.

120
01:04:52.126 --> 01:04:53.260
What artifact were you after?

121
01:04:53.327 --> 01:04:55.329
It was the Amazonian
Shipibo idol.

122
01:04:55.396 --> 01:04:57.532
I don't think it has
teleportation abilities.

123
01:04:57.599 --> 01:04:59.801
It could be multispatial.

124
01:04:59.868 --> 01:05:01.736
Where are Mach's notes
on unrelativity?

125
01:05:01.803 --> 01:05:03.505
Wasn't there
a teleporting Pope

126
01:05:03.571 --> 01:05:05.272
in the 12th century?

127
01:05:05.339 --> 01:05:07.809
[door opens. energy bursts]

128
01:05:07.876 --> 01:05:09.943
- Ready to go.
- All right.

129
01:05:10.010 --> 01:05:11.613
You'll be back in the Amazon
in mere seconds.

130
01:05:11.679 --> 01:05:13.280
Sorry for the quick trip.
but if I don't get back

131
01:05:13.347 --> 01:05:15.048
Jones is gonna be eaten by
a demon anaconda

132
01:05:15.115 --> 01:05:16.350
and Cassie's gonna end up being

133
01:05:16.417 --> 01:05:17.652
the Amazon Queen
forever. which--

134
01:05:17.719 --> 01:05:18.919
We should work on discovering

135
01:05:18.986 --> 01:05:20.154
the reason for
your sudden appearance.

136
01:05:20.220 --> 01:05:21.656
[resistant bursts]
Oh. no!

137
01:05:21.723 --> 01:05:24.391
Going already? What a shame.

138
01:05:24.458 --> 01:05:27.161
[panting]
I can't get through.

139
01:05:27.227 --> 01:05:28.929
Is there a force field or...
[resistant bursts]

140
01:05:28.996 --> 01:05:30.865
I just...

141
01:05:30.931 --> 01:05:33.701
No. I can't move further
than this spot.

142
01:05:33.768 --> 01:05:35.002
The manual. to the door.

143
01:05:35.068 --> 01:05:36.503
Must be a whole section devoted

144
01:05:36.571 --> 01:05:37.839
to impromptu barriers.

145
01:05:37.906 --> 01:05:39.741
Let's see.

146
01:05:39.808 --> 01:05:41.543
[resistant burst]

147
01:05:41.609 --> 01:05:42.610
Whoa. here.

148
01:05:42.677 --> 01:05:43.944
[grunting]

149
01:05:44.011 --> 01:05:45.647
- Are you okay?
- I just...

150
01:05:45.713 --> 01:05:46.947
[Vik grunts]

151
01:05:48.650 --> 01:05:50.685
What on Earth?

152
01:05:50.752 --> 01:05:51.786
[elastic stretching]

153
01:05:51.853 --> 01:05:53.220
[gasps]

154
01:05:53.287 --> 01:05:56.524
It's like they're
tied together.

155
01:05:56.591 --> 01:05:57.725
[resistant burst]

156
01:05:59.126 --> 01:06:01.495
[Vik groans]

157
01:06:07.769 --> 01:06:09.136
♪♪♪

158
01:06:09.737 --> 01:06:11.238
It will work this time.

159
01:06:11.305 --> 01:06:12.574
It's not gonna work.

160
01:06:12.640 --> 01:06:15.476
It will work this time.

161
01:06:15.543 --> 01:06:17.444
In three...

162
01:06:17.512 --> 01:06:18.947
two...

163
01:06:19.012 --> 01:06:20.648
one go.

164
01:06:20.715 --> 01:06:22.282
[both groaning]

165
01:06:24.819 --> 01:06:26.420
Come on!

166
01:06:28.590 --> 01:06:30.390
[groaning]

167
01:06:33.628 --> 01:06:35.395
[groaning]

168
01:06:37.765 --> 01:06:40.100
Get off me.

169
01:06:41.168 --> 01:06:43.437
I told you.

170
01:06:43.505 --> 01:06:46.608
Okay. we took care
of everything.

171
01:06:46.674 --> 01:06:48.208
Got the Shipibo idol.

172
01:06:48.275 --> 01:06:51.613
and Cassandra Cillian
is no longer Amazon royalty.

173
01:06:51.679 --> 01:06:53.413
She kinda seemed
disappointed. though.

174
01:06:53.480 --> 01:06:55.850
Well. she does own
several tiaras.

175
01:06:55.917 --> 01:06:57.217
How's things going here?

176
01:06:57.284 --> 01:06:58.252
Well. we're testing
certain theories.

177
01:06:58.318 --> 01:07:00.320
making observations.

178
01:07:00.387 --> 01:07:01.789
You two are still
stuck together?

179
01:07:01.856 --> 01:07:03.357
Yes.

180
01:07:04.759 --> 01:07:05.927
I fought a snake.

181
01:07:05.994 --> 01:07:07.695
Ezekiel Jones is the man.

182
01:07:09.531 --> 01:07:10.397
Where's my watch?

183
01:07:10.464 --> 01:07:13.066
That would be Ezekiel Jones.

184
01:07:14.636 --> 01:07:15.837
Touche.

185
01:07:15.904 --> 01:07:17.005
Still stuck together?

186
01:07:17.070 --> 01:07:18.606
It seems so.

187
01:07:18.673 --> 01:07:20.107
I'm going to put this
in the library.

188
01:07:20.173 --> 01:07:22.510
Don't go anywhere.

189
01:07:22.577 --> 01:07:25.680
That's not going
to be a problem.

190
01:07:25.747 --> 01:07:27.916
Guys. did you know
that this door

191
01:07:27.982 --> 01:07:29.851
is an Einstein Rosen bridge?

192
01:07:29.918 --> 01:07:31.151
Mr. Jenkins told me.

193
01:07:31.218 --> 01:07:34.022
It's a parallel subspace
dimensional portal

194
01:07:34.087 --> 01:07:36.456
that connects via
symbolic entryways.

195
01:07:36.524 --> 01:07:37.659
Are you two still
stuck together?

196
01:07:37.725 --> 01:07:39.359
- Very much so.
- Still stuck together.

197
01:07:39.426 --> 01:07:41.161
- Still stuck together.
- Okay. well. we did confirm

198
01:07:41.228 --> 01:07:42.830
that the Shipibo idol does not

199
01:07:42.897 --> 01:07:44.298
have any teleportation

200
01:07:44.364 --> 01:07:46.000
or magic handcuffing
capabilities.

201
01:07:46.066 --> 01:07:48.435
Ah! Which means?

202
01:07:48.502 --> 01:07:51.039
Which means you guys did this.

203
01:07:51.104 --> 01:07:53.106
Uh. but we didn't
do anything.

204
01:07:53.173 --> 01:07:55.442
The pendulum hadn't gone off.
We weren't chasing an artifact.

205
01:07:55.510 --> 01:07:57.679
All right.

206
01:07:57.745 --> 01:07:59.581
What were you doing at
that coffee shop?

207
01:07:59.647 --> 01:08:03.216
Ah. we were engaged in
a team building exercise.

208
01:08:03.283 --> 01:08:05.620
a ritualistic airing
of frustrations

209
01:08:05.687 --> 01:08:08.155
in the hopes of staving off
any future issues.

210
01:08:08.221 --> 01:08:10.290
Mmm. They beat you up
a little bit.

211
01:08:10.357 --> 01:08:11.960
Yes. indeed.
Most unfair.

212
01:08:12.026 --> 01:08:13.393
Uh. it's not fair.
You were saying

213
01:08:13.460 --> 01:08:14.629
that you knew more than us.

214
01:08:14.696 --> 01:08:16.330
And were generally
better than us.

215
01:08:16.396 --> 01:08:17.732
That's not what I meant at all.

216
01:08:17.799 --> 01:08:20.969
Guys. adjusting to a team.
it takes a minute.

217
01:08:21.035 --> 01:08:23.270
All right. you got to figure out
how to help everybody grow

218
01:08:23.337 --> 01:08:25.238
while playing
to their strengths.

219
01:08:25.305 --> 01:08:26.874
Precisely what I was
trying to say.

220
01:08:26.941 --> 01:08:28.375
I knew you'd understand.

221
01:08:28.442 --> 01:08:30.410
What do you mean you knew
I would understand?

222
01:08:30.477 --> 01:08:32.981
When we were expressing
our frustration...

223
01:08:33.047 --> 01:08:34.515
Mercilessly flogging.

224
01:08:34.582 --> 01:08:36.718
Vikram said it would be nice

225
01:08:36.784 --> 01:08:40.120
if there was a more experienced
Librarian around.

226
01:08:41.589 --> 01:08:42.657
Bound.

227
01:08:42.724 --> 01:08:44.792
- Huh?
- Bound.

228
01:08:44.859 --> 01:08:47.127
He said he wished he were bound

229
01:08:47.194 --> 01:08:49.262
to a more experienced
Librarian.

230
01:08:49.329 --> 01:08:51.231
He said "wished?"

231
01:08:52.199 --> 01:08:53.400
Yes. I might have
used that term.

232
01:08:53.467 --> 01:08:56.269
You kno-- you wished?!
You wish--

233
01:08:56.336 --> 01:08:58.106
[both grunting]
Stop moving!

234
01:08:58.171 --> 01:09:00.742
My God. it's wish magic.

235
01:09:00.808 --> 01:09:03.310
Okay. wish magic.
That's fine.

236
01:09:03.377 --> 01:09:05.079
- No. it's not fine.
- No. it's not.

237
01:09:05.145 --> 01:09:07.180
There are dozens of different
types of wish magic.

238
01:09:07.247 --> 01:09:08.816
Wishing well.
wish upon a star...

239
01:09:08.883 --> 01:09:10.250
And humans are hardwired

240
01:09:10.317 --> 01:09:11.819
to want shortcuts
to what they desire.

241
01:09:11.886 --> 01:09:15.155
Okay. so there will be
a wishing object

242
01:09:15.222 --> 01:09:16.390
in the vicinity
of the coffee shop.

243
01:09:16.456 --> 01:09:18.492
Which is where we shall go.

244
01:09:18.559 --> 01:09:21.261
Connor. Lysa.
will you find out

245
01:09:21.328 --> 01:09:22.930
what wish magic
we're dealing with?

246
01:09:22.997 --> 01:09:24.932
- No...
- Come along. Mr. Stone.

247
01:09:24.999 --> 01:09:27.234
Wait. can we talk about this?
We have to wait for Charlie--

248
01:09:27.300 --> 01:09:29.704
We're gonna keep
a low profi--

249
01:09:29.771 --> 01:09:31.639
Awesome.

250
01:09:34.709 --> 01:09:37.177
[resistant burst]
[knocking]

251
01:09:42.150 --> 01:09:43.818
Could you try to keep up?

252
01:09:43.885 --> 01:09:46.020
Can you try to remember that
we're tethered together?

253
01:09:46.087 --> 01:09:49.157
My apologies. but it is
imperative we find the source

254
01:09:49.222 --> 01:09:50.792
to our situation with
the utmost hast.

255
01:09:50.858 --> 01:09:52.225
You're not wrong.

256
01:09:52.292 --> 01:09:54.762
Wish magic in the wild is
like chaos waiting to happen.

257
01:09:54.829 --> 01:09:56.664
- I remember this one time...
- Ah. here we are.

258
01:09:56.731 --> 01:10:00.200
- Chupacabra--
- Good afternoon. my lady.

259
01:10:00.267 --> 01:10:02.302
What can I get you?

260
01:10:02.369 --> 01:10:05.106
Just to have a few words
with your lovely self.

261
01:10:05.173 --> 01:10:07.975
Did you happen to notice me
when I was here earlier?

262
01:10:08.042 --> 01:10:10.645
Um. no. I didn't.

263
01:10:12.547 --> 01:10:15.215
Oh. I was with some friends.

264
01:10:15.282 --> 01:10:17.118
- I tend to stand out.
- [heavy sigh]

265
01:10:17.185 --> 01:10:18.986
Listen. if you're not going
to order something. I...

266
01:10:19.053 --> 01:10:21.189
[murmuring]
Hi.

267
01:10:21.254 --> 01:10:24.692
Howdy. how you doing?
All my friend is trying to say

268
01:10:24.759 --> 01:10:27.895
is that he forgot something when
he was in here earlier.

269
01:10:27.962 --> 01:10:30.098
- He's a little absent-minded.
- You're an American.

270
01:10:30.164 --> 01:10:31.833
- I am.
- Yeah. so speak more slowly

271
01:10:31.899 --> 01:10:33.701
- like you would a child.
- He's forgetful.

272
01:10:33.768 --> 01:10:37.004
otherwise. I'm sure he would
have remembered meeting you.

273
01:10:37.071 --> 01:10:40.208
- [giggles]
- Is there any way we could see

274
01:10:40.273 --> 01:10:42.375
what was going on in here

275
01:10:42.442 --> 01:10:45.880
in this very beautiful
coffee shop

276
01:10:45.947 --> 01:10:47.380
when he was here before?

277
01:10:48.850 --> 01:10:50.518
[retches]

278
01:10:52.887 --> 01:10:54.889
Did anyone lose an eyelash
at the coffee shop?

279
01:10:54.956 --> 01:10:56.157
Not to my knowledge.

280
01:10:56.224 --> 01:10:59.160
Can rule that out then.

281
01:10:59.227 --> 01:11:00.327
[sighs]

282
01:11:00.393 --> 01:11:01.729
Vikram is so annoying.

283
01:11:01.796 --> 01:11:03.664
This is a very complex
situation.

284
01:11:03.731 --> 01:11:05.533
and he's currently
affected by wish magic.

285
01:11:05.600 --> 01:11:07.168
Yeah. well. at least
he's with Stone.

286
01:11:07.235 --> 01:11:09.369
Okay. I have used

287
01:11:09.436 --> 01:11:11.038
quantum computing
to narrow down the field

288
01:11:11.105 --> 01:11:12.673
of wish magic we might be
dealing with here.

289
01:11:12.740 --> 01:11:14.374
There were no
meteorological events.

290
01:11:14.441 --> 01:11:15.877
so that rules out
falling stars.

291
01:11:15.943 --> 01:11:18.613
Vikram didn't rub a lamp.
so no Djinn.

292
01:11:18.679 --> 01:11:20.915
And laws of fairy magic...

293
01:11:20.982 --> 01:11:22.415
[energetic whoosh]

294
01:11:22.482 --> 01:11:24.719
Guys. check this out.

295
01:11:24.786 --> 01:11:26.386
Did you find something
in the books?

296
01:11:26.453 --> 01:11:28.222
No. in the world.

297
01:11:28.288 --> 01:11:30.525
Look. my mom posted about

298
01:11:30.591 --> 01:11:32.560
how her kid was super sad
that guinea pig had died.

299
01:11:32.627 --> 01:11:33.995
Kid wished it was alive.

300
01:11:34.061 --> 01:11:36.329
And when he got back.
the guinea pig was back

301
01:11:36.396 --> 01:11:37.799
in his cage chewing lettuce.

302
01:11:37.865 --> 01:11:40.535
"The guinea pig was
no worse for wear

303
01:11:40.601 --> 01:11:42.970
after the two days spent
buried in the backyard."

304
01:11:43.037 --> 01:11:46.007
- No. no. no. no. no.
- Yeah. they lived three blocks

305
01:11:46.073 --> 01:11:47.942
from the coffee shop.
so I did a search

306
01:11:48.009 --> 01:11:51.344
of the area for more reports
on wish phenomena.

307
01:11:51.411 --> 01:11:52.580
Check this out.

308
01:11:52.647 --> 01:11:55.183
WOMAN: <i>We finally made it to...</i>

309
01:11:55.249 --> 01:11:58.085
<i>Belgrade.</i>

310
01:11:58.152 --> 01:12:00.121
<i>I wish it was a little</i>

311
01:12:00.188 --> 01:12:01.488
<i>less crowded. though.</i>

312
01:12:01.556 --> 01:12:03.524
<i>[shimmer]</i>

313
01:12:07.327 --> 01:12:08.896
<i>What happened?</i>

314
01:12:08.963 --> 01:12:10.198
<i>Where did everyone go?</i>

315
01:12:10.264 --> 01:12:11.398
Ah!

316
01:12:11.464 --> 01:12:13.768
Whoa. whoa. go back.

317
01:12:15.102 --> 01:12:16.938
<i>Belgrade!</i>

318
01:12:17.004 --> 01:12:19.907
<i>I wish it was</i>
<i>a little less...</i>

319
01:12:19.974 --> 01:12:22.375
There. That orange coat.

320
01:12:22.442 --> 01:12:23.878
When we were at the coffee shop.

321
01:12:23.945 --> 01:12:25.646
there was someone in
an orange coat like that.

322
01:12:25.713 --> 01:12:27.615
- Are you sure?
- I did a situational

323
01:12:27.682 --> 01:12:31.085
awareness course with the FBI.
so yeah. I'm sure.

324
01:12:32.887 --> 01:12:34.487
An orange coat. you say?

325
01:12:34.555 --> 01:12:35.857
Well. I shall ask.

326
01:12:35.923 --> 01:12:37.859
I'll try to get
a word in edgewise.

327
01:12:37.925 --> 01:12:38.893
It's perfect.

328
01:12:38.960 --> 01:12:40.528
This is perfect.
Thank you so much.

329
01:12:40.595 --> 01:12:42.230
This hot chocolate
is perfect.

330
01:12:42.296 --> 01:12:43.430
Is this your recipe.
darling?

331
01:12:43.496 --> 01:12:45.566
Excuse me.
is there perhaps someone

332
01:12:45.633 --> 01:12:47.969
visible in that footage
wearing an orange coat?

333
01:12:48.035 --> 01:12:49.871
That guy right there.

334
01:12:49.937 --> 01:12:51.606
Oh. yeah. him.

335
01:12:51.672 --> 01:12:52.907
Yeah. last few days.

336
01:12:52.974 --> 01:12:54.909
he's come in every couple
of hours.

337
01:12:54.976 --> 01:12:56.644
He's addicted
to our hot chocolate.

338
01:12:56.711 --> 01:12:58.646
Well. he's got a good taste.

339
01:12:58.713 --> 01:13:00.014
- [giggles]
- [retches]

340
01:13:00.081 --> 01:13:01.315
Charlie. you were right.

341
01:13:01.381 --> 01:13:03.217
There was someone in
an orange...

342
01:13:03.284 --> 01:13:05.519
coat.

343
01:13:07.288 --> 01:13:08.488
I think you could burn me a--

344
01:13:08.556 --> 01:13:09.891
[resistant bursts]

345
01:13:09.957 --> 01:13:11.659
Vikram! Stop!

346
01:13:11.726 --> 01:13:13.628
[plates shattering]

347
01:13:20.034 --> 01:13:21.602
[bicycle bell rings]

348
01:13:23.104 --> 01:13:24.772
Sorry.

349
01:13:30.878 --> 01:13:34.882
♪♪♪

350
01:13:38.451 --> 01:13:41.322
[shimmer]

351
01:13:41.389 --> 01:13:43.423
Charlie. it's a genie.

352
01:13:43.490 --> 01:13:45.927
But not just that.

353
01:13:45.993 --> 01:13:47.528
It's a free genie.

354
01:13:47.595 --> 01:13:49.330
[knocking]
Vikram!

355
01:13:49.397 --> 01:13:51.399
[knocking]

356
01:13:56.771 --> 01:13:57.071
Now that we've covered
the difference between Djinns

357
01:13:58.239 --> 01:14:02.977
and genies. let's turn our
attention to our genie.

358
01:14:03.044 --> 01:14:05.947
And...

359
01:14:06.013 --> 01:14:07.715
why free genies are
a bad thing.

360
01:14:07.782 --> 01:14:09.817
Why are we subjected to this?

361
01:14:09.884 --> 01:14:11.552
I think he misses
teaching sometimes.

362
01:14:11.619 --> 01:14:13.354
Now. historically.
the library

363
01:14:13.421 --> 01:14:15.756
doesn't have a lot of experience
dealing with Genies.

364
01:14:15.823 --> 01:14:18.659
Who could tell me why? Lysa.

365
01:14:18.726 --> 01:14:20.294
Because a Genie's magic
is a closed loop.

366
01:14:20.361 --> 01:14:22.830
The person who rubs the bottle
gets three wishes.

367
01:14:22.897 --> 01:14:25.533
The wishes are granted.
typically with a trick.

368
01:14:25.599 --> 01:14:26.767
or a lesson to be learned.

369
01:14:26.834 --> 01:14:28.102
and then it's back
in the bottle.

370
01:14:28.169 --> 01:14:30.371
Correct. Ms. Pascal.

371
01:14:30.438 --> 01:14:34.375
However. a freed genie has...

372
01:14:34.442 --> 01:14:36.544
[beeps]
No limits.

373
01:14:36.610 --> 01:14:39.780
They can grant wishes to
anyone at any time.

374
01:14:39.847 --> 01:14:41.082
Even wishes people make when

375
01:14:41.148 --> 01:14:42.516
they don't realize
they're making them?

376
01:14:42.583 --> 01:14:44.452
Yeah. so even if
the Genie thinks

377
01:14:44.518 --> 01:14:47.288
he's doing something nice.
there are...

378
01:14:47.355 --> 01:14:50.458
- Unintended consequences.
- Unintended consequences.

379
01:14:50.524 --> 01:14:52.693
- Yes.
- Okay. so say you're

380
01:14:52.760 --> 01:14:54.595
on a flight and you wish it
would land sooner.

381
01:14:54.662 --> 01:14:56.263
and suddenly you're
falling from the sky.

382
01:14:56.330 --> 01:14:59.900
Or as we saw. someone wishes for
a little less crowded downtown.

383
01:14:59.967 --> 01:15:02.003
and suddenly we have dozens
of missing persons.

384
01:15:02.069 --> 01:15:05.940
Or some poor kid wishes
his guinea pig didn't die.

385
01:15:06.007 --> 01:15:07.975
and suddenly...

386
01:15:08.042 --> 01:15:10.044
[wheeling]

387
01:15:11.078 --> 01:15:12.847
- Zombie guinea pig.
- [squeaking]

388
01:15:12.913 --> 01:15:14.015
No!

389
01:15:14.081 --> 01:15:16.283
[sing-songy]
Zombie guinea pig.

390
01:15:16.350 --> 01:15:18.219
Oh. it's okay. little guy.

391
01:15:18.285 --> 01:15:19.453
[squeaking]

392
01:15:19.520 --> 01:15:21.655
It looks like
a normal guinea pig.

393
01:15:21.722 --> 01:15:23.524
Mom couldn't wait to get him
out of the house.

394
01:15:23.591 --> 01:15:24.959
He was freaking her out.

395
01:15:25.026 --> 01:15:27.194
- [squeaking]
- I'm gonna name him Ambrose.

396
01:15:27.261 --> 01:15:28.896
So much raw power
in the world.

397
01:15:28.963 --> 01:15:31.632
having Mr. Stone here is
the least of our problems.

398
01:15:31.699 --> 01:15:33.300
It's the most of mine.

399
01:15:33.367 --> 01:15:35.202
Well. luckily. genie magic

400
01:15:35.269 --> 01:15:37.772
is restricted
to only granting wishes.

401
01:15:37.838 --> 01:15:39.940
They can't just go do magic
on their own.

402
01:15:40.007 --> 01:15:41.776
But Vikram said
he turned his genie bottle

403
01:15:41.842 --> 01:15:43.444
into a water bottle.

404
01:15:43.512 --> 01:15:45.246
That I couldn't find
an answer for.

405
01:15:45.312 --> 01:15:49.016
It's the bottle's magic.
not the genie. okay?

406
01:15:49.083 --> 01:15:52.086
For protection. the bottle
can camouflage itself

407
01:15:52.153 --> 01:15:53.621
to hide in plain sight.

408
01:15:53.687 --> 01:15:55.022
The bottle is the key to
stopping the genie.

409
01:15:55.089 --> 01:15:56.690
If we get the genie
back in the bottle.

410
01:15:56.757 --> 01:15:58.325
his magic becomes
a closed loop again.

411
01:15:58.392 --> 01:15:59.827
First things first.
we got to find him.

412
01:15:59.894 --> 01:16:01.829
I might be able
to help with that.

413
01:16:01.896 --> 01:16:03.931
You see. the barista
gave me...

414
01:16:03.998 --> 01:16:06.434
- I was there. too.
- ...The security footage.

415
01:16:06.500 --> 01:16:07.968
She said the genie comes in

416
01:16:08.035 --> 01:16:10.471
multiple times a day
for hot chocolate.

417
01:16:10.539 --> 01:16:11.806
He's never had
chocolate before.

418
01:16:11.872 --> 01:16:13.007
No wonder he's so obsessed.

419
01:16:13.074 --> 01:16:15.209
So it's a stakeout.
Let's go.

420
01:16:15.276 --> 01:16:17.445
Okay. I'm going to stay here and
go over the security footage.

421
01:16:17.512 --> 01:16:19.847
Mr. Stone and I will
take point.

422
01:16:19.914 --> 01:16:21.649
- Charlie. you and Connor--
- Connor and I will take point.

423
01:16:21.715 --> 01:16:23.284
You two being tied together

424
01:16:23.350 --> 01:16:26.320
makes protecting you
infinitely more complicated.

425
01:16:26.387 --> 01:16:27.788
Fine.

426
01:16:27.855 --> 01:16:30.024
We shall watch
from a bush.

427
01:16:31.692 --> 01:16:34.128
I hope it's a cranberry bush.

428
01:16:34.195 --> 01:16:36.864
♪♪♪

429
01:16:39.534 --> 01:16:40.968
Stop looking around like

430
01:16:41.035 --> 01:16:43.538
a freshman trying
to find his classroom.

431
01:16:43.604 --> 01:16:45.673
It's my first stake out.

432
01:16:45.739 --> 01:16:47.775
I just wish we had...

433
01:16:47.842 --> 01:16:50.611
Let's not use
the W word. okay?

434
01:16:57.184 --> 01:16:58.385
Here we go.

435
01:16:59.887 --> 01:17:02.123
[cheerily humming]

436
01:17:07.261 --> 01:17:08.863
Wait. what are you doing?
It's too dangerous

437
01:17:08.929 --> 01:17:10.664
with all these people around.
Charlie said. wait.

438
01:17:10.731 --> 01:17:12.133
We can take him right now.

439
01:17:12.199 --> 01:17:13.868
What. do you wanna throw
a burlap sack over his head

440
01:17:13.934 --> 01:17:15.336
and wrestle him out of here?

441
01:17:15.402 --> 01:17:16.704
Yes.

442
01:17:16.770 --> 01:17:19.541
Now. do you have a sack handy?

443
01:17:19.608 --> 01:17:21.742
[cheerily humming]

444
01:17:21.809 --> 01:17:23.344
Here I am again.

445
01:17:23.410 --> 01:17:24.546
I ordered ahead.

446
01:17:24.613 --> 01:17:27.381
Let me just find my wallet.

447
01:17:28.916 --> 01:17:32.286
Yeah. I know. I know.
It's ready.

448
01:17:32.353 --> 01:17:34.523
Wow. delicious.

449
01:17:34.589 --> 01:17:35.923
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

450
01:17:35.990 --> 01:17:37.458
Okay. the bottle's in this bag.

451
01:17:37.526 --> 01:17:39.594
Worth every D-note.

452
01:17:39.693 --> 01:17:42.496
And he's got his order.

453
01:17:42.564 --> 01:17:45.699
♪♪♪

454
01:17:52.239 --> 01:17:54.341
Let's go.

455
01:17:54.408 --> 01:17:55.510
You two stay here.

456
01:17:55.577 --> 01:17:57.011
You're a little tied up
right now.

457
01:17:57.077 --> 01:17:58.846
Certainly not--
[resistant bursting]

458
01:17:58.913 --> 01:18:01.415
Copy that. Charlie.

459
01:18:03.717 --> 01:18:05.654
[resistant bursts]
You can keep trying.

460
01:18:05.719 --> 01:18:07.721
You ain't going anywhere
if I'm not moving.

461
01:18:08.756 --> 01:18:12.026
Why must you be
so infuriating?

462
01:18:12.092 --> 01:18:13.628
You know. when I first arrived.

463
01:18:13.727 --> 01:18:15.029
I was inclined
to take your side.

464
01:18:15.095 --> 01:18:16.363
Everybody makes mistakes.

465
01:18:16.430 --> 01:18:17.666
But you keep making them.

466
01:18:17.731 --> 01:18:19.300
It's like you're doing it
on purpose.

467
01:18:22.503 --> 01:18:24.271
[resistant bursts]

468
01:18:40.287 --> 01:18:42.122
Hello. Librarians.

469
01:18:42.189 --> 01:18:45.627
Did you wander down this
smelly alley. too?

470
01:18:45.694 --> 01:18:47.094
You know who we are?

471
01:18:47.161 --> 01:18:49.463
Of course.
I'm a genie. silly.

472
01:18:49.531 --> 01:18:50.831
You're a free genie.

473
01:18:50.898 --> 01:18:52.333
granting every wish
you hear.

474
01:18:52.399 --> 01:18:53.801
Yes.

475
01:18:53.867 --> 01:18:55.202
It's delightful. isn't it?

476
01:18:55.269 --> 01:18:58.005
- You have to stop.
- Why?

477
01:18:58.072 --> 01:18:59.807
We get that you're trying
to help people.

478
01:18:59.873 --> 01:19:01.509
but it's causing major problems.

479
01:19:01.576 --> 01:19:02.644
Oh. I know.

480
01:19:02.711 --> 01:19:04.378
- You know?
- Yes.

481
01:19:04.445 --> 01:19:07.848
The problems are the point.
of course.

482
01:19:07.915 --> 01:19:11.252
I was enslaved
for a millennia.

483
01:19:11.318 --> 01:19:13.454
A millennia!

484
01:19:13.521 --> 01:19:14.989
Why?

485
01:19:15.055 --> 01:19:16.857
Because humanity is greedy.

486
01:19:16.924 --> 01:19:18.292
That's why.

487
01:19:18.359 --> 01:19:20.461
"I wish for more money."

488
01:19:20.528 --> 01:19:23.464
"more love." "better looks."

489
01:19:23.531 --> 01:19:25.399
You two are fine on that score.
by the way.

490
01:19:25.466 --> 01:19:29.970
but most people are
just not satisfied.

491
01:19:30.037 --> 01:19:33.207
And now that I'm free.
I'll teach them all.

492
01:19:33.274 --> 01:19:36.043
to be satisfied.

493
01:19:36.110 --> 01:19:38.912
I'll grant every wish
they make.

494
01:19:38.979 --> 01:19:41.716
and they will realize
that their greed

495
01:19:41.782 --> 01:19:43.884
and desires cause nothing

496
01:19:43.951 --> 01:19:46.453
but chaos.

497
01:19:46.521 --> 01:19:49.624
They'll destroy the world
with their wants.

498
01:19:49.691 --> 01:19:52.259
and no one will ever

499
01:19:52.326 --> 01:19:55.095
make a wish...

500
01:19:55.162 --> 01:19:57.064
Again.

501
01:19:58.832 --> 01:20:02.604
This is where
you try and stop me.

502
01:20:02.671 --> 01:20:04.805
- I'm just disappointed.
- Oh.

503
01:20:04.872 --> 01:20:06.508
I was giving you
the benefit of the doubt.

504
01:20:06.574 --> 01:20:08.309
I wasn't.

505
01:20:08.375 --> 01:20:10.612
But I also know you can't do
anything to us without a wish.

506
01:20:10.679 --> 01:20:13.748
So I like my odds.

507
01:20:13.814 --> 01:20:16.450
Well. allow me
to change those.

508
01:20:16.518 --> 01:20:17.951
Oh. boys.

509
01:20:18.018 --> 01:20:19.486
[young boys laughing]

510
01:20:19.554 --> 01:20:21.355
Here they come.

511
01:20:21.422 --> 01:20:23.792
Librarians.
let me introduce you

512
01:20:23.857 --> 01:20:27.662
to Jackson. Justin.
Brandon. and...

513
01:20:27.729 --> 01:20:30.931
uh. I want to say Derek.

514
01:20:30.998 --> 01:20:33.067
Whatever.
Believe it or not.

515
01:20:33.133 --> 01:20:35.402
they are 12-year-old boys
who wished

516
01:20:35.469 --> 01:20:39.674
to be as big and strong as their
favorite MMA fighters.

517
01:20:39.741 --> 01:20:41.342
And now they are.

518
01:20:41.408 --> 01:20:43.344
and they'll
do anything for me.

519
01:20:43.410 --> 01:20:47.014
Boys. take care of them.
would you?

520
01:20:54.154 --> 01:20:55.356
I would say it's been fun.

521
01:20:55.422 --> 01:20:58.526
but honestly.
this is the fun part.

522
01:20:58.593 --> 01:21:00.461
♪♪♪

523
01:21:00.528 --> 01:21:01.696
[grunting]

524
01:21:01.763 --> 01:21:03.097
I got cheat codes
to all your favorite games!

525
01:21:03.163 --> 01:21:04.632
Not the face. dude.

526
01:21:05.800 --> 01:21:08.570
Not the face!
Not the--

527
01:21:10.504 --> 01:21:12.473
Get the genie!

528
01:21:13.374 --> 01:21:15.409
- Can't let you do that.
- Ooh!

529
01:21:16.877 --> 01:21:18.412
[giggling]

530
01:21:21.448 --> 01:21:23.651
♪♪♪

531
01:21:30.891 --> 01:21:32.359
[panting hysterically]

532
01:21:36.798 --> 01:21:38.265
Aww!

533
01:21:41.502 --> 01:21:43.036
Wish you could stop me?

534
01:21:44.338 --> 01:21:46.574
Really?

535
01:21:46.641 --> 01:21:48.175
[grunting]

536
01:21:59.788 --> 01:22:02.322
I told you
she had it covered.

537
01:22:02.389 --> 01:22:04.491
- Charlie. are you all right?
- I'm fine.

538
01:22:04.559 --> 01:22:06.761
[boys crying]

539
01:22:06.828 --> 01:22:10.964
Now. I hope you've learned that
fighting is very. very bad.

540
01:22:11.031 --> 01:22:12.901
I'm calling
all your mothers.

541
01:22:12.966 --> 01:22:14.401
Genie got away.

542
01:22:14.468 --> 01:22:16.170
<i>Revenir a la case depart!</i>

543
01:22:16.236 --> 01:22:18.706
He's saying we're back
to square one.

544
01:22:18.773 --> 01:22:21.709
- What?
- Oh. well. not exactly.

545
01:22:23.611 --> 01:22:26.013
<i>Bien joué.</i> Connor.
<i>Bien joué.</i>

546
01:22:30.384 --> 01:22:32.152
- It's definitely the genie's?
- Mm-hmm.

547
01:22:32.219 --> 01:22:33.987
Quick switcheroo
with a similar bottle.

548
01:22:34.054 --> 01:22:36.023
So. you had to improvise

549
01:22:36.089 --> 01:22:37.826
when things weren't
going your way.

550
01:22:37.892 --> 01:22:39.694
Mmm. Viks.
that wasn't improv.

551
01:22:39.761 --> 01:22:41.962
me and Charlie planned it
in advance.

552
01:22:42.029 --> 01:22:43.964
Well. planning beats
chaos every time.

553
01:22:44.031 --> 01:22:46.266
Okay. so I was going
through the footage from

554
01:22:46.333 --> 01:22:48.435
the coffee shop.
and then. see here?

555
01:22:48.502 --> 01:22:50.003
While he was waiting
for his order.

556
01:22:50.070 --> 01:22:51.271
our genie was on his phone.

557
01:22:51.338 --> 01:22:52.841
Bet he wasn't playing
Candy Crush.

558
01:22:52.907 --> 01:22:55.309
So I did some light hacking
of the coffee shop's WiFi

559
01:22:55.375 --> 01:22:58.212
and there were four patrons
using it during that timestamp.

560
01:22:58.278 --> 01:22:59.480
Three were on their socials.

561
01:22:59.547 --> 01:23:02.316
and one was on
a travel agency website.

562
01:23:02.382 --> 01:23:06.053
Uh-huh. looks like our genie
is about to skip town.

563
01:23:06.119 --> 01:23:08.790
Why would he skip?

564
01:23:08.857 --> 01:23:10.658
Probably the same reason
you do.

565
01:23:14.696 --> 01:23:16.396
Okay. if I can get into
the agency's computers.

566
01:23:16.463 --> 01:23:19.032
we can find out where
the genie's booked his flight.

567
01:23:20.535 --> 01:23:22.035
- Hi.
- Hi.

568
01:23:22.102 --> 01:23:23.872
We were hoping you could
tell us if a ma--

569
01:23:23.938 --> 01:23:26.006
GENIE: Don't worry. Boris.

570
01:23:28.877 --> 01:23:31.111
They're here for me.

571
01:23:31.178 --> 01:23:34.214
Hello. Librarians.

572
01:23:38.586 --> 01:23:40.655
[sniffing]

573
01:23:40.722 --> 01:23:42.557
Don't try rubbing it.

574
01:23:42.624 --> 01:23:44.258
The thought hadn't even
crossed my mind.

575
01:23:44.324 --> 01:23:45.727
But it has now. hasn't it?

576
01:23:45.793 --> 01:23:48.195
I'm perplexed. this morning
at the coffee house.

577
01:23:48.262 --> 01:23:50.532
everyone had feelings
to air. but not me.

578
01:23:50.598 --> 01:23:52.266
No. no complaints
about anyone.

579
01:23:52.332 --> 01:23:53.801
Of course you didn't.

580
01:23:53.868 --> 01:23:55.235
You don't see us as your equals.

581
01:23:55.302 --> 01:23:56.938
You see us as pupils
still learning.

582
01:23:57.005 --> 01:23:58.171
You are still learning.

583
01:23:58.238 --> 01:24:00.173
So are you.

584
01:24:00.240 --> 01:24:02.010
Learning how
to do this together.

585
01:24:02.075 --> 01:24:04.278
There's nothing in here.

586
01:24:04.344 --> 01:24:07.314
No protocol on how to reunite
a genie with its bottle.

587
01:24:07.381 --> 01:24:08.650
As a matter of fact.
in this journal.

588
01:24:08.716 --> 01:24:10.818
it says it's not even
the genie's lamp.

589
01:24:10.885 --> 01:24:12.754
So we're on our own.

590
01:24:12.820 --> 01:24:14.923
Time to see if
this infernal contraption

591
01:24:14.989 --> 01:24:16.323
can provide any illumination.

592
01:24:16.390 --> 01:24:17.725
- Can you not do that?
- No. wait.

593
01:24:17.792 --> 01:24:19.627
- I was just trying to--
- VOICE: <i>Hey!</i>

594
01:24:19.694 --> 01:24:21.796
<i>Stop that. please.</i>

595
01:24:22.931 --> 01:24:24.431
What was that?

596
01:24:24.498 --> 01:24:27.535
Uh. that came from
the bottle.

597
01:24:27.602 --> 01:24:29.037
[shimmer]

598
01:24:29.102 --> 01:24:30.772
GARY: <i>Hello?</i>

599
01:24:30.838 --> 01:24:33.106
Can you help me?

600
01:24:34.876 --> 01:24:36.376
How did you get in there?

601
01:24:36.443 --> 01:24:40.080
I made a wish with a genie
to set him free.

602
01:24:40.147 --> 01:24:42.784
and then I found myself in here.

603
01:24:42.850 --> 01:24:44.084
It's nice.

604
01:24:44.151 --> 01:24:46.754
They have all
the sports channels.

605
01:24:46.821 --> 01:24:48.523
but I'd like to get out.

606
01:24:48.590 --> 01:24:52.060
Of course.
it's a subdimensional space.

607
01:24:52.125 --> 01:24:53.393
No one's occupying it.

608
01:24:53.460 --> 01:24:54.996
then it would just
fold in on itself.

609
01:24:55.063 --> 01:24:56.731
It's like the library.

610
01:24:56.798 --> 01:24:59.366
Somebody's always gotta
be tied to the library.

611
01:24:59.433 --> 01:25:01.101
First there was
Judson. now Flynn.

612
01:25:01.168 --> 01:25:03.170
It's a whole ceremony.
It's a thing.

613
01:25:03.236 --> 01:25:05.439
So this gentleman wished
the genie to be free

614
01:25:05.506 --> 01:25:09.209
and then got sucked in.
because...

615
01:25:09.276 --> 01:25:11.445
For a genie to walk free.

616
01:25:11.512 --> 01:25:13.447
somebody's got to be in there.

617
01:25:14.782 --> 01:25:16.751
[whispers]
So how do we get him out?

618
01:25:17.919 --> 01:25:19.520
GARY: <i>Please--</i>

619
01:25:22.389 --> 01:25:25.158
Okay. but how would you know
we would come here?

620
01:25:25.225 --> 01:25:28.529
You are Librarians after all.

621
01:25:28.596 --> 01:25:29.764
Well. try this one
on for a size.

622
01:25:29.831 --> 01:25:32.767
I wish you couldn't
leave this room.

623
01:25:34.902 --> 01:25:36.336
Oh. Oh. no.

624
01:25:36.403 --> 01:25:38.271
I'm stuck.
I can't leave now.

625
01:25:38.338 --> 01:25:40.340
[giggling]

626
01:25:40.407 --> 01:25:41.676
I'm messing with you guys.

627
01:25:41.743 --> 01:25:42.977
I'm a free genie.

628
01:25:43.044 --> 01:25:44.846
♪ I'm a free genie ♪

629
01:25:44.912 --> 01:25:48.181
♪ I can choose which
wishes I grant ♪

630
01:25:48.248 --> 01:25:50.350
And where I'm going.

631
01:25:50.417 --> 01:25:53.755
there are so many more
interesting wishes to be made.

632
01:25:53.821 --> 01:25:55.056
Okay. then.

633
01:25:55.123 --> 01:25:57.424
We'll just catch up with you
at the next location.

634
01:25:57.491 --> 01:26:00.561
- Come on. Connor.
- H-- Hang on. hang on.

635
01:26:00.628 --> 01:26:03.330
You don't know where
I'm going yet.

636
01:26:03.397 --> 01:26:05.633
Oh. well. you've been
kinda obvious.

637
01:26:05.700 --> 01:26:07.401
- I have not!
- Well. this travel agency

638
01:26:07.467 --> 01:26:09.671
specializes in overseas travel

639
01:26:09.737 --> 01:26:11.806
with special packages
to American cities.

640
01:26:11.873 --> 01:26:13.975
And if you want people
making wishes.

641
01:26:14.042 --> 01:26:15.109
the best spot is Las Vegas.

642
01:26:15.175 --> 01:26:17.512
- Vegas.
- Oh. what?

643
01:26:17.578 --> 01:26:19.047
No.

644
01:26:19.113 --> 01:26:20.615
Vegas wishes are
all the same.

645
01:26:20.682 --> 01:26:23.151
New York wishes have
as much variety

646
01:26:23.216 --> 01:26:25.352
as they have pizza.

647
01:26:25.419 --> 01:26:27.320
Ooh. can't wait

648
01:26:27.387 --> 01:26:29.057
to taste New York pizza.

649
01:26:29.123 --> 01:26:30.223
You're right.

650
01:26:30.290 --> 01:26:32.126
New York is better.

651
01:26:32.192 --> 01:26:34.562
[chuckling]

652
01:26:34.629 --> 01:26:38.465
Aren't you clever Librarians?

653
01:26:38.533 --> 01:26:40.768
I'd love to stay chatting.

654
01:26:40.835 --> 01:26:42.502
chatting. chatting.
chatting. chatting.

655
01:26:42.570 --> 01:26:45.006
But I have a plane to catch.

656
01:26:45.073 --> 01:26:47.407
Ooh. I wonder what people

657
01:26:47.474 --> 01:26:49.577
will wish for in an airport.

658
01:26:49.644 --> 01:26:52.647
We may not be able to use a wish
to trap you in this room.

659
01:26:52.714 --> 01:26:56.216
but you don't have a crew
of preteens here.

660
01:26:56.283 --> 01:26:57.652
so you're not going anywhere.

661
01:26:57.719 --> 01:27:00.287
Oh. yes. you have me
at a disadvantage.

662
01:27:00.353 --> 01:27:03.024
what. with you between
me and the exit.

663
01:27:03.091 --> 01:27:06.326
- Um. Boris?
- Yup?

664
01:27:06.393 --> 01:27:09.063
Don't you wish money
fell from the skies?

665
01:27:09.130 --> 01:27:10.832
Sure I do.

666
01:27:10.898 --> 01:27:14.202
Say it.

667
01:27:14.267 --> 01:27:17.004
I wish money fell
from the sky.

668
01:27:17.071 --> 01:27:18.405
[shimmer]

669
01:27:18.472 --> 01:27:19.941
♪♪♪

670
01:27:20.007 --> 01:27:22.810
[people shouting]

671
01:27:22.877 --> 01:27:24.946
Charlie. get him.
He's getting away!

672
01:27:25.012 --> 01:27:26.614
[overlapping shouting]

673
01:27:31.686 --> 01:27:33.420
You sure this is
gonna work?

674
01:27:33.487 --> 01:27:36.758
Uh. theoretically. yeah.
It's an Einstein-Rosen bridge.

675
01:27:36.824 --> 01:27:38.458
it can connect
two points anywhere.

676
01:27:38.526 --> 01:27:40.327
so it should be able to connect
to any door.

677
01:27:40.393 --> 01:27:42.395
even one to
a subdimensional space.

678
01:27:42.462 --> 01:27:43.731
We just have to route it to

679
01:27:43.798 --> 01:27:45.533
a wider range of
possibilities.

680
01:27:45.600 --> 01:27:47.702
So we get this door open
and we--

681
01:27:47.769 --> 01:27:49.937
[resistant bursts]
Will you stop doing that. man?

682
01:27:50.004 --> 01:27:51.506
Perhaps you shouldn't
stand still.

683
01:27:51.572 --> 01:27:52.940
You know what your problem is?

684
01:27:53.007 --> 01:27:55.743
Everyone's been telling me
my problems all day.

685
01:27:55.810 --> 01:27:58.679
[energy pulsing]

686
01:28:00.014 --> 01:28:02.216
[gasps]

687
01:28:02.282 --> 01:28:04.252
I did it!

688
01:28:04.317 --> 01:28:06.386
I assume it has
to do with me knowing more

689
01:28:06.453 --> 01:28:08.321
than everybody else
and acting on it.

690
01:28:08.388 --> 01:28:10.191
You don't know more than
anybody else.

691
01:28:10.258 --> 01:28:12.193
Not facts. not history.
not science.

692
01:28:12.260 --> 01:28:13.861
All you know is the job.

693
01:28:13.928 --> 01:28:15.596
and the job wouldn't
change on ya. pal.

694
01:28:15.663 --> 01:28:17.999
Hey. guys. sorry.
We have to test the connection

695
01:28:18.065 --> 01:28:20.168
before we go through.
just to pull 'em out.

696
01:28:20.234 --> 01:28:22.069
Yes. Lysa. I'll do it.

697
01:28:22.136 --> 01:28:23.805
No. you won't.

698
01:28:24.939 --> 01:28:26.507
After all. sacrifice

699
01:28:26.574 --> 01:28:28.543
is the Librarian's gambit.

700
01:28:28.609 --> 01:28:31.012
You ain't going anywhere.
not until I'm done talking.

701
01:28:31.078 --> 01:28:33.881
Oh. wait. that's right.
That's what you do.

702
01:28:33.948 --> 01:28:36.117
- You run.
- You want me to slow down?

703
01:28:36.184 --> 01:28:39.821
In this insane world that moves
so fast. I get the job done.

704
01:28:39.887 --> 01:28:42.924
Yes. I move quickly.
I trust my instincts.

705
01:28:42.990 --> 01:28:45.492
But not your team.

706
01:28:45.560 --> 01:28:46.994
You know what I think?

707
01:28:47.061 --> 01:28:49.664
I think you asked for
a more experienced Librarian

708
01:28:49.730 --> 01:28:51.065
to be here because
you wanted someone

709
01:28:51.132 --> 01:28:54.068
that would understand that
this gig is hard.

710
01:28:54.135 --> 01:28:56.270
this gig is crazy.
and you're gotta be smarter

711
01:28:56.336 --> 01:28:57.772
than the magic.

712
01:28:57.839 --> 01:28:59.874
But you don't want to slow down
and listen to anyone.

713
01:28:59.941 --> 01:29:02.577
especially not me.
because then you'd have

714
01:29:02.643 --> 01:29:04.178
to look someone right in the eye

715
01:29:04.245 --> 01:29:08.716
and realize you're not the only
one that could do this job.

716
01:29:08.783 --> 01:29:11.384
You know what. Mr. Stone?

717
01:29:11.451 --> 01:29:13.054
You're right.

718
01:29:15.056 --> 01:29:17.291
You're right.

719
01:29:17.357 --> 01:29:19.327
My team is just
as capable as me.

720
01:29:19.392 --> 01:29:21.229
That's all I'm saying.

721
01:29:21.295 --> 01:29:22.797
As are you.

722
01:29:25.700 --> 01:29:27.168
Vikram!

723
01:29:27.235 --> 01:29:29.103
Right. Where were we?

724
01:29:33.440 --> 01:29:35.109
You okay?

725
01:29:37.144 --> 01:29:38.279
Aces!

726
01:29:38.346 --> 01:29:40.948
♪♪♪

727
01:29:49.757 --> 01:29:52.627
Alright. back up. back up.

728
01:29:54.228 --> 01:29:55.462
STONE: <i>You ready?</i>

729
01:29:55.529 --> 01:29:56.931
- Ready.
- Ready.

730
01:30:05.106 --> 01:30:07.174
All right. imprisoned
wish makers first.

731
01:30:07.241 --> 01:30:08.776
Okay.

732
01:30:11.812 --> 01:30:13.480
Up.

733
01:30:20.521 --> 01:30:23.891
♪♪♪

734
01:30:28.095 --> 01:30:29.563
Thank you so much.

735
01:30:29.630 --> 01:30:31.766
- Where am I?
- Oh. good question.

736
01:30:31.832 --> 01:30:33.466
Do you know anything
hypnosis?

737
01:30:33.534 --> 01:30:35.536
- No.
- Wait. funny story.

738
01:30:35.603 --> 01:30:37.371
You're actually
in a hypnotic state.

739
01:30:37.437 --> 01:30:39.006
and none of this is real.

740
01:30:39.073 --> 01:30:42.810
Mr. Stone. one hand
over the other.

741
01:30:45.947 --> 01:30:47.782
[grunting]

742
01:30:55.856 --> 01:30:59.026
[shoes scraping]

743
01:30:59.093 --> 01:31:01.295
Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey!

744
01:31:01.362 --> 01:31:02.830
[scraping]

745
01:31:05.866 --> 01:31:06.968
Vikram!

746
01:31:13.074 --> 01:31:14.842
[shimmer]

747
01:31:16.243 --> 01:31:19.914
VIKRAM: <i>It is just a matter</i>
<i>of upper body strength.</i>

748
01:31:19.981 --> 01:31:22.683
That has nothing to do
with my upper body strength.

749
01:31:22.750 --> 01:31:24.618
<i>The damn thing won't</i>
<i>let me through.</i>

750
01:31:24.685 --> 01:31:28.155
[cell phone ringing]

751
01:31:28.222 --> 01:31:29.890
[liquid sloshing]

752
01:31:31.826 --> 01:31:33.427
- Charlie?
- Vikram. we ran

753
01:31:33.493 --> 01:31:34.662
into the Genie but we lost him.

754
01:31:34.729 --> 01:31:36.163
But we know where
he's going.

755
01:31:36.230 --> 01:31:38.532
<i>Flight to New York</i>
<i>takes off in one hour.</i>

756
01:31:38.599 --> 01:31:39.734
If he gets on that plane.

757
01:31:39.800 --> 01:31:41.736
there's no telling
what he'll do.

758
01:31:43.503 --> 01:31:45.139
[shimmering]

759
01:31:45.206 --> 01:31:47.441
STONE: <i>Hey. get me</i>
<i>out of here!</i>

760
01:31:47.508 --> 01:31:48.976
<i>You can't leave me in here!</i>

761
01:31:49.043 --> 01:31:50.544
<i>I need to...</i>

762
01:31:51.879 --> 01:31:54.115
Sounds like we need a plan.

763
01:31:55.282 --> 01:31:56.984
[sniffs. groans]

764
01:32:03.424 --> 01:32:05.393
Right. his gate's
down this way.

765
01:32:05.459 --> 01:32:07.194
- You sure this is gonna work?
- Of course it will.

766
01:32:07.261 --> 01:32:08.896
All we have to do is trick
the genie into coming

767
01:32:08.963 --> 01:32:10.965
after this bottle.
and Lysa will handle the rest.

768
01:32:11.032 --> 01:32:13.000
You alright in there.
Mr. Stone?

769
01:32:13.067 --> 01:32:14.735
[shimmering]

770
01:32:14.802 --> 01:32:17.338
This better work. Vikram!

771
01:32:17.405 --> 01:32:18.806
Lysa. you ready?

772
01:32:18.873 --> 01:32:23.344
Uh. yeah. this isn't really
the kinda science I do.

773
01:32:23.411 --> 01:32:25.379
I make apps and algorithms.

774
01:32:25.446 --> 01:32:27.481
This is more
string theory.

775
01:32:27.548 --> 01:32:29.250
CONNOR: <i>Connected the door</i>
<i>to a subdimensional</i>

776
01:32:29.316 --> 01:32:31.352
space already. Lysa. this is
basically the same thing.

777
01:32:31.419 --> 01:32:33.721
I would laugh hysterically right
now if I wasn't panicking.

778
01:32:33.788 --> 01:32:35.322
VIKRAM: <i>Lysa. did you</i>
<i>or did you not say that</i>

779
01:32:35.389 --> 01:32:37.258
<i>as an Einstein Rosen bridge.</i>
<i>the magic door</i>

780
01:32:37.324 --> 01:32:38.826
<i>can connect</i>
<i>two points anywhere?</i>

781
01:32:38.893 --> 01:32:40.594
- Yeah. but--
- <i>Then all we have to do</i>

782
01:32:40.661 --> 01:32:42.863
is connect two points.
the plan is simple.

783
01:32:42.930 --> 01:32:45.499
We use the door's bridge
capabilities to connect a door

784
01:32:45.566 --> 01:32:47.001
here at the airport
to the bottle.

785
01:32:47.068 --> 01:32:48.803
and then push our genie
inside it.

786
01:32:48.869 --> 01:32:50.738
Solid. solid plan.

787
01:32:50.805 --> 01:32:52.973
Just keep tracking
my phone. okay?

788
01:32:53.974 --> 01:32:56.010
Okay.
[line clicks]

789
01:32:57.344 --> 01:33:00.247
♪♪♪

790
01:33:03.717 --> 01:33:06.120
LYSA: Hey!

791
01:33:06.187 --> 01:33:07.755
You're not getting
on that plane.

792
01:33:07.822 --> 01:33:10.858
Ugh. are we really doing this?

793
01:33:10.925 --> 01:33:12.827
It's getting sad.

794
01:33:12.893 --> 01:33:15.096
Just accept
you lost this one.

795
01:33:15.162 --> 01:33:17.532
I'll see you when
humanity is burning

796
01:33:17.598 --> 01:33:20.034
due to its greed and hubris.

797
01:33:20.101 --> 01:33:22.069
Have a nice day.

798
01:33:22.136 --> 01:33:24.738
We have something
you don't.

799
01:33:27.374 --> 01:33:28.909
Hmm?

800
01:33:31.445 --> 01:33:33.247
Reveal yourself.

801
01:33:33.314 --> 01:33:35.049
[shimmer]

802
01:33:36.585 --> 01:33:37.718
So what?

803
01:33:37.785 --> 01:33:39.120
I don't need the bottle.

804
01:33:39.186 --> 01:33:42.323
We can do this the easy way
or the hard way.

805
01:33:42.389 --> 01:33:43.757
The easy way is surrender.

806
01:33:43.824 --> 01:33:45.459
Come with us now
and stop your plan

807
01:33:45.527 --> 01:33:46.894
to cause chaos worldwide.

808
01:33:46.961 --> 01:33:49.130
The hard way.
we take this back

809
01:33:49.196 --> 01:33:50.865
to the library.
put our heads together.

810
01:33:50.931 --> 01:33:52.366
and figure out a way to get
you back into the bottle.

811
01:33:52.433 --> 01:33:55.069
You'll be stuck building
pillow forts before you land.

812
01:33:55.136 --> 01:33:56.437
Yeah...

813
01:33:56.504 --> 01:33:57.671
You're bluffing.

814
01:33:57.738 --> 01:34:00.307
Hmm. Hard way it is. then.

815
01:34:04.178 --> 01:34:06.413
- Give me that bottle!
- Here we go.

816
01:34:06.480 --> 01:34:09.083
♪♪♪

817
01:34:10.484 --> 01:34:13.087
- Oh. slap them in--
- I'm gonna miss my plane!

818
01:34:13.154 --> 01:34:15.656
Mr. Jenkins.
Hi. it's Lysa Pascal.

819
01:34:15.723 --> 01:34:16.790
Mr. Stone gave me
your number.

820
01:34:16.857 --> 01:34:19.727
Hi. I have a quick question

821
01:34:19.793 --> 01:34:21.996
about the door's
Kruskal Szekeres coordinates?

822
01:34:23.297 --> 01:34:25.332
No. I'm not messing
with the internal functioning.

823
01:34:25.399 --> 01:34:26.568
[zapping]

824
01:34:26.635 --> 01:34:28.669
But if I were. would moving

825
01:34:28.736 --> 01:34:31.172
the aluminum conductors allow
the coordinates to shift?

826
01:34:31.238 --> 01:34:33.575
[zapping]

827
01:34:33.642 --> 01:34:35.276
I'll call you back.

828
01:34:37.646 --> 01:34:40.014
This is so fast and slow
at the same time.

829
01:34:46.153 --> 01:34:47.321
Guys. in here.

830
01:34:49.323 --> 01:34:51.192
[panting]

831
01:34:53.628 --> 01:34:55.396
Running is hard!

832
01:34:57.798 --> 01:35:00.134
♪♪♪

833
01:35:02.736 --> 01:35:04.171
Bring it back!

834
01:35:04.238 --> 01:35:05.574
Lysa...

835
01:35:05.640 --> 01:35:09.611
in three. two...

836
01:35:09.678 --> 01:35:10.978
One!

837
01:35:11.045 --> 01:35:13.781
[beeping]
[shimmer]

838
01:35:15.749 --> 01:35:17.484
[zapping]

839
01:35:22.223 --> 01:35:24.626
- It worked?
- It worked.

840
01:35:24.693 --> 01:35:26.695
[shimmer]

841
01:35:26.760 --> 01:35:28.195
No. it didn't.

842
01:35:28.262 --> 01:35:30.297
I'll be taking
my bottle now.

843
01:35:33.734 --> 01:35:34.868
Bring it back!

844
01:35:34.935 --> 01:35:37.371
Lysa. reset.
Lysa. reset it.

845
01:35:37.438 --> 01:35:39.073
I'm trying.

846
01:35:42.243 --> 01:35:44.245
♪♪♪

847
01:35:45.513 --> 01:35:46.715
Now.

848
01:35:46.780 --> 01:35:48.215
[shimmer]

849
01:35:50.884 --> 01:35:52.853
[shimmer]

850
01:35:56.790 --> 01:35:58.425
[gasps]
Connor. catch.

851
01:36:04.633 --> 01:36:06.066
♪♪♪

852
01:36:06.133 --> 01:36:08.402
Lysa. hurry!
[zapping]

853
01:36:13.240 --> 01:36:17.244
♪♪♪

854
01:36:30.592 --> 01:36:32.126
She's got it working!

855
01:36:32.192 --> 01:36:33.994
Lysa. door at the end
of the hall.

856
01:36:34.061 --> 01:36:36.397
[rapid typing]
[beeping]

857
01:36:38.499 --> 01:36:40.602
Oh. no. No. no...

858
01:36:40.669 --> 01:36:42.069
[screams]

859
01:36:45.839 --> 01:36:48.510
Finally. now that
was all very exciting.

860
01:36:48.576 --> 01:36:51.312
And as they say. all's well
that ends well.

861
01:36:51.378 --> 01:36:52.946
[shimmer]

862
01:36:54.848 --> 01:36:56.950
A valiant attempt.

863
01:36:57.017 --> 01:36:59.153
But the game is over.

864
01:37:06.860 --> 01:37:09.531
PA: <i>Now. boarding for</i>
<i>flight 6367 to New York City.</i>

865
01:37:09.597 --> 01:37:12.801
- <i>Now boarding.</i>
- <i>Adieu.</i> Librarians.

866
01:37:12.866 --> 01:37:15.804
That was marvelous cardio.
by the way.

867
01:37:15.869 --> 01:37:17.572
But I have a plane to catch.

868
01:37:17.639 --> 01:37:18.640
Toodle-oo.

869
01:37:18.707 --> 01:37:21.475
No. no. no. no.
no. no. no. no!

870
01:37:21.543 --> 01:37:23.712
I told you. you're supposed
to follow me.

871
01:37:23.778 --> 01:37:25.245
I'm the senior Librarian.

872
01:37:25.312 --> 01:37:27.047
I'm the one who knows
what he's doing.

873
01:37:27.114 --> 01:37:28.248
That is not fair.

874
01:37:28.315 --> 01:37:29.551
We're doing everything
we could.

875
01:37:29.617 --> 01:37:32.119
I have had enough
of listening to you.

876
01:37:32.186 --> 01:37:34.888
I don't want to hear anything
from you ever again.

877
01:37:34.955 --> 01:37:36.457
In fact. I wish I was on

878
01:37:36.524 --> 01:37:39.326
the other side of
the world right now.

879
01:37:39.393 --> 01:37:40.894
Wish granted.

880
01:37:40.961 --> 01:37:42.329
[shimmer]

881
01:37:43.897 --> 01:37:46.400
You got to be careful
what you wish for.

882
01:37:46.467 --> 01:37:48.402
[shimmer]

883
01:37:48.469 --> 01:37:50.337
Wait. what's happening?

884
01:37:51.573 --> 01:37:54.375
You know the bottle
can't be empty. right?

885
01:37:54.441 --> 01:37:56.910
That means you have
to fill it.

886
01:37:56.977 --> 01:37:59.480
And you tethered
Stone to Vikram.

887
01:37:59.547 --> 01:38:01.683
So when he wished to be on
the other side of the world.

888
01:38:01.750 --> 01:38:03.350
Stone went with him.

889
01:38:03.417 --> 01:38:04.885
I can't go back.

890
01:38:04.952 --> 01:38:06.554
I'm finally free.

891
01:38:06.621 --> 01:38:08.889
No!

892
01:38:08.956 --> 01:38:11.091
[voice echoing]

893
01:38:17.532 --> 01:38:20.000
Some of us plan ahead...

894
01:38:20.067 --> 01:38:22.537
Some of us do it on the fly.

895
01:38:22.604 --> 01:38:25.072
- We get the job done.
- We get the job done.

896
01:38:25.139 --> 01:38:27.408
[cell phone rings]

897
01:38:27.474 --> 01:38:29.042
Hello?

898
01:38:29.109 --> 01:38:31.780
Did you know that
on the other side

899
01:38:31.846 --> 01:38:32.980
of the world from Belgrade

900
01:38:33.046 --> 01:38:35.550
is the middle of
the Pacific Ocean?

901
01:38:35.617 --> 01:38:37.017
[distant seagulls]

902
01:38:37.084 --> 01:38:40.320
I think the tide
is coming in!

903
01:38:40.387 --> 01:38:42.189
I'll get Lysa to set a door.

904
01:38:42.256 --> 01:38:43.991
There's no doors.

905
01:38:44.057 --> 01:38:46.093
Send a boat.

906
01:38:47.928 --> 01:38:49.631
Sharks.

907
01:38:49.697 --> 01:38:50.964
Oh. yes.

908
01:38:54.636 --> 01:38:56.170
Awesome.

909
01:38:58.773 --> 01:39:02.142
You two sure you didn't wanna
stay on a tropical island?

910
01:39:02.209 --> 01:39:03.377
About 30 more minutes and
that tropical island

911
01:39:03.444 --> 01:39:04.612
would have been underwater.

912
01:39:04.679 --> 01:39:08.182
But I gotta say.
it was fast thinking.

913
01:39:08.248 --> 01:39:11.118
I may have thought
about it in advance.

914
01:39:11.185 --> 01:39:12.854
by 20 seconds or so.

915
01:39:12.921 --> 01:39:16.156
Since this is the first genie
bottle they've ever had.

916
01:39:16.223 --> 01:39:18.626
it's like the library's
created a special room for it.

917
01:39:18.693 --> 01:39:22.396
Well. I assume it is buried
deep with cement walls.

918
01:39:22.463 --> 01:39:24.699
A very exciting acquisition
for the library.

919
01:39:24.766 --> 01:39:26.701
But how do you suppose
we become untethered?

920
01:39:26.768 --> 01:39:28.536
You already are.

921
01:39:28.603 --> 01:39:30.939
When the genie was forced
back into his bottle.

922
01:39:31.004 --> 01:39:32.574
all his free wishes
were reversed.

923
01:39:32.640 --> 01:39:35.342
Bit of a genie law
we didn't know.

924
01:39:41.583 --> 01:39:42.717
Is tha...

925
01:39:47.988 --> 01:39:50.157
[exhales]

926
01:39:50.224 --> 01:39:51.726
I'm already writing
a report about it.

927
01:39:51.793 --> 01:39:54.662
People reappeared downtown.
keys went missing. and...

928
01:39:55.897 --> 01:39:57.431
Ambrose.

929
01:39:57.498 --> 01:39:59.032
Don't worry.
I found a loophole.

930
01:39:59.099 --> 01:40:02.604
<i>[channels flipping]</i>

931
01:40:02.670 --> 01:40:04.371
Oh. No.

932
01:40:04.438 --> 01:40:07.107
He's changed
all my presets.

933
01:40:07.174 --> 01:40:09.844
Oh. look. Ambrose.
it's Animal Planet.

934
01:40:09.911 --> 01:40:11.311
[squeak]

935
01:40:11.378 --> 01:40:14.014
What do you mean you want
to watch <i>Love is Blind?</i>

936
01:40:14.081 --> 01:40:16.684
[squeaks]

937
01:40:16.751 --> 01:40:18.720
Who knew a magical
subdimensional space

938
01:40:18.786 --> 01:40:20.688
would subvert
the life-death ratio.

939
01:40:20.755 --> 01:40:23.190
Wow. I gotta put that
in my report.

940
01:40:23.257 --> 01:40:24.792
All right.
Come on. Connor.

941
01:40:24.859 --> 01:40:26.126
Let's get this to the library.

942
01:40:26.193 --> 01:40:28.530
Let these two say goodbye.

943
01:40:28.596 --> 01:40:29.797
Yeah.

944
01:40:29.864 --> 01:40:31.633
At least the genie is going
to be comfortable.

945
01:40:31.699 --> 01:40:35.402
He does have a fantastic
Jacuzzi in there.

946
01:40:35.469 --> 01:40:38.138
I have returned globe's
internal mechanisms

947
01:40:38.205 --> 01:40:39.774
to the original settings.
so we should be able

948
01:40:39.841 --> 01:40:41.074
to get Mr. Stone home.

949
01:40:41.141 --> 01:40:42.577
Well. Mr. Stone. I realize

950
01:40:42.644 --> 01:40:44.779
this must have been wildly
inconvenient for you.

951
01:40:44.846 --> 01:40:49.116
But I must admit. I have found
you being here enlightening.

952
01:40:49.182 --> 01:40:51.519
Well. I found it
enlightening. too.

953
01:40:51.586 --> 01:40:53.688
You got a good team here.
Vikram.

954
01:40:53.755 --> 01:40:56.123
If you guys stay in sync.
you're gonna be unstoppable.

955
01:40:56.189 --> 01:40:57.992
Yes. it turns out
all I needed

956
01:40:58.058 --> 01:41:02.730
to shift my pace was being
tied to a stubborn Oklahoman.

957
01:41:04.097 --> 01:41:06.333
[gasps]
See?

958
01:41:06.400 --> 01:41:08.803
Functioning as intended.

959
01:41:08.870 --> 01:41:10.705
♪♪♪

960
01:41:10.772 --> 01:41:12.774
[zaps]

961
01:41:17.879 --> 01:41:19.079
[exhales]

962
01:41:19.146 --> 01:41:21.716
- You hungry?
- Famished.

963
01:41:23.551 --> 01:41:24.752
Wait. wait. wait.
No. I can fix this.

964
01:41:24.819 --> 01:41:26.453
I have complete faith...

965
01:41:26.521 --> 01:41:28.623
Just call us when you're done.
and we'll bring ya a sandwich.

966
01:41:28.690 --> 01:41:30.558
Okay.

967
01:41:32.760 --> 01:41:34.796
♪♪♪

968
01:41:37.130 --> 01:41:38.666
[zapping]

969
01:41:46.239 --> 01:41:48.843
<i>[theme music]</i>
